{
  "id": "defanging_an_ip_address",
  "title": "Defanging an IP Address",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "String"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Given a valid (IPv4) IP <code>address</code>, return a defanged version of that IP address.</p> <p>A <em>defanged IP address</em> replaces every period <code>\".\"</code> with <code>\"[.]\"</code>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> address = \"1.1.1.1\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> \"1[.]1[.]1[.]1\"\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> address = \"255.100.50.0\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> \"255[.]100[.]50[.]0\"\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li>The given <code>address</code> is a valid IPv4 address.</li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
  "method": {
    "name": "defangIPaddr",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "address",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
